    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d328">

                <pb facs="0321" n="309" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg309"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">870.811/235: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-04-29T15:00:00+02:00">April 29, 1941—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:17 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1637. My 4477, October 27, 1 p.m. 1940.<anchor n="76" xml:id="d328-f1"/> It is
                    announced in Berlin that the seat of the International Danube Commission has
                    been moved from Belgrade to Orsova, the “Serbian” representative and
                    administrative personnel have been excluded from the Commission, the transit
                    fees at the Iron Gate are in future payable in marks rather than Swiss francs
                    and German has been designated the “official language in the administration of
                    the Iron Gate”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d328-f1" n="76" xml:id="d328-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed, but see telegram No. 670, October 26, 1940, from the Minister in
                    Rumania, <ref target="frus1940v01#pg_524">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1940, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 524</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
